# Save three times in the middle of a session and keep playing after each one.
#
#   tools/headless.sh tools/keys/save-continue.keys 1
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. Registry::SaveGroup is not read-only: it turns every data
# block POINTER in every object of the group into that block's HANDLE while it
# writes, then swaps them back. A session that saves and carries on is
# therefore the only session that can show a restore which does not put back
# exactly what it took. tools/keys/smoke.keys and tools/keys/explore.keys
# contain no save command at all, so neither of them has any power over that
# question. See bd inc-i0r.
#
# ESC b is the System Menu's [b] Save and Continue (src/Player.cpp:734-747).
# It is the only save the game offers that does not also end the session.
# READ THE WARNING IN tools/keys/explore-mage.keys BEFORE MOVING IT: ESC opens
# that menu rather than cancelling anything, [a] is Save and Quit, and a stray
# ESC therefore ends the run and still exits 0. Each ESC b below sits straight
# after a screen dump, where the screen is known and no other menu is open.
#
# Save and Continue costs the player one tick of game time
# (src/Player.cpp:746 sets Timeout = 1), so this script and its twin
# tools/keys/save-continue-nosave.keys do NOT play the same game. The twin
# exists to be compared against this one on ONE binary, not to match it.
#
# LENGTH. About 110 player commands after character generation. Two limits set
# that: the game autosaves itself every 200 commands (src/Player.cpp:159), which
# would put a save into the no-save twin as well, and bd inc-dhc records that a
# long session stops repeating exactly from one run to the next.

@include chargen.keys

@dump:arrival

DOWN*4 RIGHT*4 UP*4 LEFT*4
s*3     # search

@dump:pre-save-1

ESC b   # System Menu -> Save and Continue

@dump:post-save-1

DOWN*4 RIGHT*4 UP*4 LEFT*4
.*5     # rest

@dump:mid-1

ESC b

@dump:post-save-2

RIGHT*4 DOWN*4 LEFT*4 UP*4
s*3 .*5

@dump:mid-2

ESC b

@dump:post-save-3

LEFT*4 UP*4 RIGHT*4 DOWN*4
s*3 .*5

@dump:final

@quit
